^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-08-24 10:59] observe — current identifiers greedily retain dots, current grammar skips most whitespace, current line-dialect preprocessing rewrites source before lexing, and current parse APIs retain every generated event.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:00] decide — call the deterministic semantic relation binding affinity; reserve spacing resonance for measured or workspace-tuned nonsemantic ranking and projection signals.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:01] decide — classify gaps as tight, open, cadence, or episode; preserve raw trivia and spans; collapse width only within a class unless a versioned semantic migration is requested.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:02] decide — semantic association profiles, parse-product requests, tooling resonance, and projection budgets are separate axes. Only the declared association profile may change AST or ONF.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:03] decide — parser speed comes from minimal products, suppressible instrumentation, content-addressed reuse, and sparse indexes over one kernel rather than tool-specific grammars.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:04] taste — do not grow already-large parser, normalizer, CLI, formatter, or LSP files; extract named modules whose types disclose the invariant they enforce.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:05] clarify — filenames mentioned while wondering about preference learning were placeholders, not proposed examples, roles, or canonical style surfaces.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:06] decide — no filename, path ordering, or ambient source document carries formatting authority; any future source-derived evidence must be explicitly registered and revision-aware.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:07] decide — make indentation, soft operator gaps, line placement, clustering, folding, and safe transforms retunable through one small workspace policy with deterministic layers and per-rule consequence previews.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:08] wonder — versioned format profiles and migration receipts may support a healthier engineering culture by giving collaborators stable names for conventions, upgrade effects, and compatibility choices without coupling them to a monolithic language release.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:09] decide — format migrations expose plan, apply, and verify as separate idempotent stages with preconditions, reversibility status, compatibility windows, and durable receipts.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:10] taste — pair concise scaffolding with effective-rule explanation, profile diffs, task-oriented migration guidance, complete reference, and decision notes; defaults should be easy to adopt and easy to interrogate.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:30] decide — exchange with independent projects uses capabilities, revisions, gap reports, workload shapes, missing questions, and consequence receipts; consumer identity and domain grammar stay outside the shared kernel.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:31] decide — retain a useful zero-annotation floor, then let optional feature annotations earn adoption through concrete recognizability, navigation, or projection benefits.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:32] revise — environment compatibility and leaf/public build radius belong to package-iteration-radius; gap tooling consumes those receipts rather than diagnosing machine agreement as syntax.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:45] observe — the first implementation slice now preserves exact inter-token surface spans, classifies tight/open/cadence/episode gaps, and retains tight dotted identifiers with explicit segment metadata while returning trailing and repeated dots to operator or connector matchers.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:46] decide — parser event and runtime trace policies change retained disclosure only; dedicated diagnostics and semantic/runtime products remain invariant, and generated-versus-retained counts expose the cost floor.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:47] decide — resolved [qualified_token]: keep a.b.c as IDENTIFIER plus segment metadata for this compatibility slice; do not introduce a second qualified-path token before association and corpus evidence.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:48] revise — inspect.spacing/1 is an observational product projected as bounded table, Spw card, or JSON envelope; it does not activate syntax.gap-affinity/1 or workspace style authority.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:55] verify — cdd0b40a lands exact gap products, dotted identifier segments, parse event policies, and semantic-invariance fixtures in the portable Seed package.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:56] verify — 8d454ad6 lands runtime trace depth, generated/retained receipts, policy-aware hot-cache identity, and the CLI→runtime composite project reference.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:57] verify — 211d7653 lands inspect.spacing/1 table/Spw/JSON projections and a reader-facing compatibility/cost note; Seed, runtime, CLI, type, Spw, and documentation gates pass.
 >>[2026-08-24 11:58] revise — the observational increment is ready for review while the plan remains active at association semantics; formatting migrations, local-style evidence, and generator suppression remain later evidence-gated work.
 >>[2026-08-24 12:00] decide — bound the next tooling slice to tokens, structure, and trace products over one portable progressive protocol; index and semantic depths remain later capabilities rather than empty placeholders.
 >>[2026-08-24 12:01] taste — a progressive claim requires stage records to leave when their product becomes available; buffered final output may be a sequence but may not masquerade as time-to-first-useful output.
 >>[2026-08-24 12:02] decide — every source product names included fields, omissions, executed stages, revision, sequence, completeness, and elapsed time; shallow lex questions stop before grammar work.
}

